      <activity id="6ebc9539-046d-524f-bfc1-4efaae46833b" activityNameId="cc363f00-9550-5c16-a3f7-e73390d06836" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cadmium sulphide, semiconductor-grade, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cadmium sulphide, semiconductor-grade, at plant
This datasets describes the production of high-grade cadmium sulphide (99.99%) from cadmium and sulfuric acid. This purity of cadmium sulphide can be used in the production of thin film solar cells. ;
CAS number: 001306-23-6; 
Formula: CdS; 
UUID: 575aa608-ed9c-3c86-b1a9-3f25f4aa9cc3
The energy consumption, emissions and transports are estimated.
Location: Production in US
Technology: Production of cadmium sulphide by hydrometallurgical process
Time period: patents
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature and own estimations 
Extrapolations: Energy consumption is extrapolated from CdCl due to lack of data and similarity of processes
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_575aa608-ed9c-3c86-b1a9-3f25f4aa9cc3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
